{
  "format": "clementina-mia-indexes",
  "version": 1,
  "count": 256,
  "notes": [
    "Owners: programs, the MIA firmware's input, video, sd and audio subsystems, and the ROM kernel (kernel.inc names its ids KIDX_*).",
    "MIA sets the default of each firmware id at reset (default.start is the current and default address, the limit is start + length). Every other id resets to all zeros.",
    "Programs may use the firmware ids; the kernel re-seeks them before each use, so their current address does not survive a kernel call. Never change $F0-$FF.",
    "name is the MIA header #define and docName the name MIA's docs print; for a run of ids (count > 1) both name the first id, and id + n is entry n."
  ],
  "flagBits": [
    {
      "bit": 0,
      "name": "R_STP_ENA",
      "description": "Step after the window's data port is read."
    },
    {
      "bit": 1,
      "name": "W_STP_ENA",
      "description": "Step after the window's data port is written."
    },
    {
      "bit": 2,
      "name": "STP_DIR",
      "description": "Step direction: 0 forward, 1 backward."
    },
    {
      "bit": 3,
      "name": "WRAP_ENA",
      "description": "Wrap when the current address crosses the configured range."
    },
    {
      "bit": 4,
      "name": "WRAP_IRQ",
      "description": "Raise the window's wrap IRQ flag when wrapping."
    }
  ],
  "ids": [
    {
